ills (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 7th District is an open seat this cycle after Republican incumbent Cory Mills lost his primary to Ryan Elijah, who now faces Democrat Bale Dalton. The district leans Republican by about five points, and most expert raters call the race Lean R, though a few see it as a Tossup or even a Democratic flip. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-three chance.\n\nThe race's clearest signal is money: Dalton has raised nearly $1.4 million with about $450,000 in outside support, while Elijah has raised under $400,000 and drawn little outside help so far. With no reliable general-election polling available, the race rests on fundamentals, and it sits close to even with a slight Republican tilt heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4211, "margin": -1.21}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4651, "margin": -1.0}]}